/-!
# Unramified radical extensions generated by `p`-independent units

Let `𝒪` be a valuation subring of a field `Ω` whose residue field has exponential
characteristic `p`, and let `F → Ω` be a field. Let `θ i` (`i ∈ ι`, finite) be elements of `Ω`
with `θ i ^ p ^ n = u i ∈ F` of value `1`, such that the residues of the `u i` are
"`p ^ n`-independent" over the residue field of `F`. Then the monomials
`∏ i, θ i ^ E i`, `0 ≤ E i < p ^ n`, are residually independent over `F`: the extension
`F(θ)` is unramified of degree `p ^ (n * #ι)` and its values are values of `F`.

## Main definitions

- `Field.PowIndependent q b`: the monomials `b ^ E`, `0 ≤ E i < q`, are linearly independent
  over the subfield of `q`-th powers (for `q = p` this is `p`-independence).
- `Valuation.ResiduallyPowIndependent v F q u`: the residual analogue for a family `u` of
  elements of `F`.

## Main statements

- `Field.PowIndependent.pow`: `p`-independence implies `p ^ n`-independence.
- `Valuation.residuallyPowIndependent_of_powIndependent`: residual `q`-independence from
  `q`-independence of the residues, when `F` is the fraction field of a local ring `R` with
  `𝒪 ∩ F = R`.
- `ValuationSubring.residuallyIndependent_prod_pow`: the monomials in the `θ i` are residually
  independent.
- `IntermediateField.mem_span_prod_pow_of_mem_adjoin`: `F(θ)` is spanned by these monomials.
- `ValuationSubring.exists_valuation_eq_of_mem_adjoin`,
  `ValuationSubring.basisProdPow`, `ValuationSubring.finrank_adjoin_eq`: consequences.
-/

@[expose] public section

